  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing sixteen songs in Grinnell, Iowa, on November 2, 2007 [1]. The setlist includes “Wild Sage,” “Slow West Vultures,” and “New Monster Avenue,” with the latter experiencing a PA outage that is not a recording flaw [1]. John Darnielle stepped away from the microphone to sing unamplified during several tracks, though this did not reduce audience chatter [1]. The performance features “September 15, 1983,” a track with only two archived performances, and “Orange Ball of Love,” which appears in eleven archived shows [1]. “Orange Ball of Hate/new song” is also included, having been absent from the setlist for over eight years prior [1]. This is the only available recording of the event, with a documented lineage [1]. A listener review of this specific file notes that while the show sounded great, the amount of talking in the mix is unbearable, including full cell phone conversations [2]. The recording is rated two out of five by one user [1]. It is the 113th of 467 archived shows for the band [3].",
